@page "/reports"

<PageTitle>Reports</PageTitle>

<div class="dashboard-page">
    <div class="page-heading">
        <h1 class="h2 mb-1">Reports</h1>
        <p class="text-secondary mb-0">Browse generated markdown reports for the selected project.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="card shadow-sm mb-4">
        <div class="card-body">
            <h2 class="h4 mb-1">Legacy.Native / Completed</h2>
            <p class="text-secondary mb-0">Reports are available because markdown generation has completed for this project.</p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="row g-4">
        <div class="col-xl-3">
            <div class="card shadow-sm h-100">
                <div class="card-body">
                    <h2 class="h5 mb-3">Available Reports</h2>
                    <div class="list-group">
                        <a class="list-group-item list-group-item-action active" href="#">memory-leak-report.md</a>
                        <a class="list-group-item list-group-item-action" href="#">performance-report.md</a>
                        <a class="list-group-item list-group-item-action" href="#">resource-cleanup-report.md</a>
                        <a class="list-group-item list-group-item-action" href="#">native-lifetime-report.md</a>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="col-xl-9">
            <div class="card shadow-sm h-100">
                <div class="card-body report-reader">
                    <h2># memory-leak-report.md</h2>
                    <h3>Summary</h3>
                    <p>Potential subscription retention was found when retry logic reconnects after cancellation windows.</p>

                    <h3>Findings</h3>
                    <ul>
                        <li>Issue type: Memory leak risk</li>
                        <li>File / function if available: SessionCache / ReconnectAsync</li>
                        <li>Why this is a problem: retained handlers may keep worker state alive longer than intended.</li>
                        <li>Suggested fix direction: centralize disposal and align cancellation with unsubscribe flow.</li>
                    </ul>

                    <h3>Evidence</h3>
                    <p>The rule flow inspected scope entry files and followed calls into RetryCoordinator and WorkerSession.</p>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>
